# Every link out asks first

A link to another origin is drawn with `ExternalLink` from `shared-components/ExternalLink.tsx`. It is the one code path for leaving the site: a new tab, `rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"`, and, while the links setting asks (the chat tab's `ask before leaving`, `settings.linkWarning`, on by default), the leave-site word first (`#leave-site`: the site's name, the whole address, `don't ask again`). A plain click, a cmd/ctrl/shift click and a middle click all ask.

- `from` is the word's first sentence: who put the link there (`the streamer put this link on their page, not this site.`). Leave it out for a link this site chose; the word says `this link goes to another site.`
- Where the `<a>` can't be swapped (a component that owns its anchor), take `useExternalLink(href, from)`: spread `onClick` and `onAuxClick` on the anchor, draw `dialog` beside it, and give it `target="_blank"` and `rel={EXTERNAL_REL}`.
- A link on this origin (a relative route, `/api/oauth/...`) is internal: a router `Link`, or an `<a>` as it was. `ExternalLink` lets a same-origin href through with no word, so a href that may be either is safe to give it.
- No `target="_blank"` anchor, no `window.open`, no `location.href =` to another origin anywhere else. Not even for a site we trust: the setting is the viewer's, and it covers every link out.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — leaves the site past the setting
<a href={link.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{word}</a>
window.open(link.url, '_blank');

// ✅ GOOD
<ExternalLink href={link.url} from={`${name} put this link here, not this site.`}>{word}</ExternalLink>

// ✅ GOOD — an anchor drawn by something else
const out = useExternalLink(href);
<a href={href} target="_blank" rel={EXTERNAL_REL} onClick={out.onClick} onAuxClick={out.onAuxClick}>…</a>
{out.dialog}
```
